   This is some code to analyze the NN behavior. 
   The purpose actually is mostly to change the python code for fortran code, 
   for people who are not familiar with python

   We will take the example as specificied in parameter.py.example:

----------------------------------
   codedir='/ssd/linwang/ALL_ML_CODE/ML_FRAME_WORK_vdw/workdir'
   trainSetDir='./train_data'
   fortranFitSourceDir='/ssd/linwang/ALL_ML_CODE/ML_FRAME_WORK_vdw/fit'
   fitModelDir='./fitmodel'
   genFeatDir='/ssd/linwang/ALL_ML_CODE/ML_FRAME_WORK_vdw/gen_feature'
   mdImageFileDir='./MD'           

  dir_work = os.path.join(fitModelDir,'NN_output/')
  d_nnEi  = os.path.join(dir_work,'NNEi/')
  d_nnFi  = os.path.join(dir_work,'NNFi/')
  f_Einn_model   = d_nnEi+'allEi_final.ckpt'
  f_Finn_model   = d_nnFi+'Fi_final.ckpt'
  f_data_scaler = d_nnFi+'data_scaler.npy'
  f_Wij_np  = d_nnFi+'Wij.npy'
-------------------------------------------------
 This parameter.py and main.py are setting in the "current" directory ">". 
 Under this current directory, there are an few sub-dir: fitmodel, MD, train_data
 fitmodel will contain the NN model, and MD will have the MD result, train_data will store the MOVEMENT for training. 
-------------------
 More specifically, we have:
 /fitmodel/NN_output/NNFi, which contains the already trained NN model files: data_scaler.npy, Wij.npy
 data_scaler.npy is the a(i) and b(i) for converting the input feat(i):  feat(i)*a(i)+b(i), note: feat(i) is without PCA
 Wij.npy contains the W(i,j,layer) and B(j) (shift) for the NN model. 
 (step 1)
 use: /fitmodel/NN_output/NNFi>python3 read_Wij.py > Wij.txt       
      to get Wij.txt
 use: /fitmodel/NN_output/NNFi>python3 read_scaler.py > scaler.txt       
      to get scaler.txt
     (how ever, for scaler.txt, need to modify it a little bit, make it looks like:
      288
      0.00000000e+00 0.00000000e+00 0.00000000e+00 0.00000000e+00
      0.00000000e+00 0.00000000e+00 0.00000000e+00 0.00000000e+00
      .....
      0.00000000e+00 0.00000000e+00 0.00000000e+00 0.00000000e+00
      288
      0.00000000e+00 0.00000000e+00 0.00000000e+00 0.00000000e+00
      0.00000000e+00 0.00000000e+00 0.00000000e+00 0.00000000e+00
      .....
      0.00000000e+00 0.00000000e+00 0.00000000e+00 0.00000000e+00
      )

 copy Wij.txt and scaler.txt to /fitmodel
 -----------------------------------
 (step 2) 
  Do a NN_MD simulation using NN model: isRunMd_nn=True (in parameters.py)
  Need to prepare atom.config in /MD
  You might need to have other files like vdw_fitB.ntype in /fitmodel
  run: >python3 main.py
  It will generate the file: /MD/md
 (step 3) 
  copy /MD/md to /train_data/md
  go to /train_data/md, move MOVEMENT to MOVEMENT.orig, use convert_MOVEMENT.r  to 
  convert the MOVEMENT.orig to MOVEMENT (the normal PWmat style). 
  (I was told there is a parameters.py option to output this style directly, but I didn't find it). 
------------------------------------------
 (step4) 
  set isCalcFeat=True
      isFitLinModel=True
  in parameters.py, run: >python3 main.py
  It will generate the feature and its derivative file dfeat.fbin.FtypeX  in train_data/md. 
  It will also (is FitLinModel=True) generate many other necessary files in /fitmodel 
 -----------------------------------------
 (step5)
  Now, in /fitmodel, you can run: TEST_NN.r. 
  It will use the feature generated above, run the NN model inside the TEST_NN. 
  The results will be output in energyL.pred.1. It should be exactly the same as the one generated from NN_MD


 


      

     >ptython3

